        "original_id": "ae7a5c53-7759-53c9-9ce7-bff17c891349",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: \"What's It Gonna Be\"\n- People: H \"Two\" O, Selim Ben Rabha, Simon McDevitt, Platnum, Aaron Evers, Mina Poli, Michelle McKenna\n- Concepts: bassline, UK garage\n- Places: Sheffield\n\nFacts:\n- Bassline is a type of music related to UK garage that originated in Sheffield in the early 2000s.\n- Bassline is sometimes referred to as bassline house, Niche, or 4x4.\n- \"What's It Gonna Be\" is a bassline song.\n- H \"Two\" O performed \"What's It Gonna Be\" with the British three-person bassline vocal group Platnum.\n- H \"Two\" O is a duo consisting of Selim Ben Rabha, also known as \"Solution,\" and Simon McDevitt, also known as \"Oz.\"\n- Selim Ben Rabha and Simon McDevitt also go by the names \"Hit 'Em\" and \"Hard.\"\n- Platnum consists of Aaron Evers, Mina Poli, and Michelle McKenna.",
